    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d865">

                <pb facs="1277" n="1261" xml:id="pg1261"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/7–2849</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Telephone Conversation, by the Deputy
                        Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Rusk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-28">July 28,
                        1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I told Mr. Connelly<anchor n="1" xml:id="d865-f1"/> that Ambassador Elath would
                    probably bring up today the question of retaining the arms embargo on Israel and
                    the Arab States. I said that Ralph Bunche had recommended to the Security
                    Council that the various truce resolutions be rescinded and that the Security
                    Council proceed on the basis of the armistice agreements. I told Mr. Connelly
                    that the Secretary of State would wish to discuss this matter very carefully
                    with the President and that the Secretary hopes that the President will make no
                    commitment to Ambassador Elath prior to the Secretary’s talk with the
                    President.</p>
                <p>Mr. Connelly said that he would take care of the matter and see to it that the
                    President “just listens”. He stated that he would need nothing in writing, that
                    my telephone call was sufficient.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d865-f1" n="1" xml:id="d865-f1-content">
                <p>Matthew J. Connelly, Secretary to President Truman.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
